-- Core set-theoretic and functional foundations that the rest of the
-- collection builds on.


-- The foundational `Declares`: `\set` requires an abstract membership relation
-- (`\\abstract` stands for "no further reduction obligation"), and enables
-- reducing membership on coerced set-builder literals through `memberOf`.
[\set]
Declares: X
Requires:
. capability: x_ "in" X :-> \\abstract
Enables:
. from: Y ::= {y__ : ...}
  capability: x_ "in" X :<->: x_ memberOf Y
Appendix:
. called: "set"
Id: "5c194a16-3f2b-4a32-9a03-6fbafb40a8df"


-- A `Declares` target may state a spec relation, which every value of the
-- defined type inherits.
[\element:of{X}]
Declares: x "in" X
when: X is \set
Appendix:
. called: "element of $X?$"
Id: "85df16c5-71d3-4e68-b87c-bbb3a85e2df8"


-- A function type describes call behavior with parenthesized spec literals on
-- both sides, using `_` for each parameter.
[\function:on{A}:to{B}]
Declares: f(x__) is (_ "in" A) -> (_ "in" B)
when: A, B is \set
Appendix:
. called: "function from $A?$ to $B?$"
. written: "A? \rightarrow B?"
Id: "98fa5602-43ab-4c75-b505-1795fa6884c8"


-- An infix command, written `\.name./` between its operands, defining the
-- Cartesian product as a coerced set builder.
[A \.cross./ B]
Defines: X := \set@{(a_, b_) : a_ "in" A; b_ "in" B}
when: A, B is \set
Appendix:
. called: "Cartesian product of $A?$ and $B?$"
. written: "A+? \times B+?"
Id: "674ead6f-ab2b-4682-b1a2-1921630d7b52"


-- Set union and intersection defined as coerced set-builder expressions.
[A \.union./ B]
Defines: U := \set@{x_ : x_ "in" A; x_ "in" B}
when: A, B is \set
Appendix:
. called: "union of $A?$ and $B?$"
. written: "A+? \cup B+?"
Id: "f1a2b3c4-1111-4aaa-8bbb-000000000001"


-- An operator-form target states its type about the operator itself, so `*` is
-- a binary operation taking two elements of `X` and returning an element of `X`.
[\operation:on{X}]
Declares: x_ * y_ is (_ "in" X, _ "in" X) -> (_ "in" X)
when: X is \set
Appendix:
. called: "binary operation on $X?$"
Id: "da1c3fe8-35fc-46b0-95ff-63ec39bfd5ef"


-- The identity function on any set, with `expresses:` specifying its action on
-- every element of `X`.
[\identity:on{X}]
Defines: f(x__) is \function:on{X}:to{X}
when: X is \set
expresses:
. forAll: x "in" X
  then: f(x) = x
Appendix:
. called: "the identity function on $X?$"
. written: "\operatorname{id}_{X?}"
Id: "3c86ff2d-f2e5-4b70-acb6-5c8502af9fe4"


-- Function composition, illustrating multi-parameter `when:` requirements and
-- an `expresses:` equation characterizing the composite at every point.
[g \.compose./ f]
Defines: h(x__) is \function:on{A}:to{C}
using:
. A, B, C is \set
when:
. f is \function:on{A}:to{B}
. g is \function:on{B}:to{C}
expresses:
. forAll: x "in" A
  then: h(x) = g(f(x))
Appendix:
. called: "composition of $g?$ and $f?$"
. written: "g+? \circ f+?"
Id: "f1a2b3c4-1111-4aaa-8bbb-000000000002"
